' PICTURE SHOW
' Two 120-colour pictures for the ColecoVision, written in Amy by Claude,
' 2026: a test of Amy's `120 colors on` and of kit/c120 (the converter).
'
' Each picture is two 6 KB VRAM banks that trade jobs every frame (patterns
' one frame, colours the next); the eye mixes the two frames. The picture
' fills the two lower screen thirds (256 x 128); the top third stays black,
' as in the historical 120C demos (see kit/c120/c120.py for why).
'
' Controls: either button shows the other picture. Keypad not used.
' Pictures: a sunset harbour (drawn for this demo, sunset.html) and the
' Lamplighter box art (games/lamp/box).

